        "reading_checked": "If the chart title is the authoritative trend classification for the routing task, then the literal word 'Decreasing' in that title supports the decline-response route. (Applies only if the title is intended to override or summarize the plotted series for the decision.)",
        "evidence": "The necessary condition is that the title is the 'authoritative trend classification' or intended to override the plotted series. The public task instructions direct the user to 'Review the Town Z new-tourist trend dashboard... as the evidence source' and 'choose the follow-up route'. The dashboard includes both the title and the plotted line. There is no explicit instruction or policy table stating that the title text overrides the visual data. Therefore, the condition that the title is the sole or overriding authority is not met by the visible evidence.",
